Done. Round gen_r2 complete for gen_rader — summary of what happened:

**Diagnosis (the round's lever):** the natural 31³ layout made the in-place x-pass a 4K-aliasing trap — row stride 961×16 B ≡ 3088 mod 4096 means a store to row j+4 lands on exactly the low-12 address bits of the next chunk's load of row j — and misaligned every access (15376 ≡ 16, 496 ≡ 48 mod 64: line splits throughout). Mechanism borrowed from gen_pfa_large r1 / ice L23_rader's mod-4096 rule.

**Fix shipped:** the chain now runs on a fully padded private state — z-rows 31→32 complex, planes →1148 complex (≡124 mod 256, chosen closed-form so the first 4K collision sits at row distance 33, outside the 31-row system). Every access in every pass is 64B-aligned, the z-pass is 8 uniform quads/plane (the pad row is provably-zero), y/x/map are tail-free, and the state+padded-c working set (1.14 MB) stays L2-resident. The create() self-check now also gates one padded chain step against the dense reference, so a stride bug can't ship. Same-window ladder: 95.95 → 91.3 (plane pad) → **86.6** (full alignment), −9.7%; the sched-pressure attribute was tried and lost badly (131.6, +44% — negative recorded). All gates verified by hand on the node: single 4.06e-16, chain m=140 2.56e-14 (B=16) / 1.92e-14 (B=1), two-step 1.63e-15 (18× margin), bit-identical repeats.

**One-liner:** Fully-padded/aligned in-place Rader-31 chain (anti-4K plane pitch 1148, z-rows→32) — **86.6 µs/step batched (B=16), 99.7 µs at B=1 (core-ramp-elevated; code path batch-invariant)** on the node, rel L2 4.06e-16 single / 2.56e-14 graded chain (tol 1e-10).
